{"id":"u-2b4fdd4d-71aa-4fb7-9870-dc7cca6e0bb7","src":"community","title":"Valhalla","author":"João Marques","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ponGZP-valhalla","desc":"Valhalla is a high-effort hypertrophy program built around a Torso / Legs / Arms rotation, with the goal of producing high-quality hard sets without accumulating unnecessary junk volume.\n\nThe split is designed to run on a 3-days-on, 1-day-off rotating schedule:\nTorso A → Legs A → Arms A → Rest → Torso B → Legs B → Arms B → Rest → repeat\n\nIt is intentionally not tied to a Monday-to-Sunday calendar. If a session is missed, there is no need to reshuffle the week or skip ahead—simply continue with the next scheduled session when you return. The rotation picks up exactly where you left off.\n\nThe program is designed to be run in blocks of roughly 7 hard weeks followed by 1 deload week. This is not a rigid rule: if fatigue starts clearly creeping in earlier, such as reduced performance, persistent soreness, lower motivation, joint irritation, or difficulty producing normal force, a deload can be taken sooner, for example in week 5 or 6.\n\nDuring the deload week, reduce training volume substantially (approximately 50%, as prescribed in the program) and use roughly 70–80% of normal working loads, keeping several reps in reserve and avoiding failure, grinders, rest-pause work, and other high-fatigue techniques.\n\nThe listed volume should also be treated as adjustable rather than mandatory. If recovery starts to suffer or a session becomes excessively fatiguing, exercises prescribed for 3 sets can be reduced to 2 sets as needed. The goal is not to complete the highest possible number of sets; the goal is to maintain good effort, good execution, and productive stimulus across the work that is performed.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-11T17:17:25.369Z","variations":[{"name":"default","day